  "question": {
    "text": "<p>If one mole of an ideal gas at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> is allowed to expand reversibly and isothermally (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>) its pressure is reduced to one-half of the original pressure (see figure). This is followed by a constant volume cooling till its pressure is reduced to one-fourth of the initial value <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Then it is restored to its initial state by a reversible adiabatic compression (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>). The net workdone by the gas is equal to:</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/bb1ac53f-4e50-4654-bd79-095a8834618a-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 237px;\" /></p>",
